{"name":"Rudraksha Beads","hex":"#894e45","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rudraksha","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The dried seed of a large evergreen broad-leaved tree, Elaeocarpus ganitrus, which is traditionally used as prayer beads in Hinduism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rudraksha"},{"term":"beads","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of bead"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beaded necklace."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beads"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rudraksha","blocks":[{"text":"A rudraksha are the dried stones or seeds of the genus Elaeocarpus specifically, Elaeocarpus ganitrus. These seeds are used as prayer beads for Hindus and Buddhists. When they are ripe, rudraksha stones are covered by a blue outer fruit so they are sometimes called \"blueberry beads\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/RudrakshaBeads.jpg/330px-RudrakshaBeads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rudraksha"},{"title":"Bead","blocks":[{"text":"A bead is a small, decorative object that is formed in a variety of shapes and sizes of a material such as stone, bone, shell, glass, plastic, wood, or pearl and with a small hole for threading or stringing. Beads range in size from under 1 mm to over 1 cm in diameter."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/45/Beads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bead"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/RudrakshaTree.jpg/500px-RudrakshaTree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/RudrakshaTree.jpg/1280px-RudrakshaTree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thu